      "updated_at": "2026-02-10T22:25:23Z",
      "body": "What should happen if the CSV reader subsequently encounters a row with a null in a field it determined to be non nullable? \n\nIf we inferred Non nullable i think it would error\n\nSo by inferring Nullable the CSV writer is being tolerant of more inputs and will error on fewer of them\n\nWe could add some flag to change this behavior if it was warranted\n\nAnother alternative would be for your application to review the data that was parsed and if there are no nulls ajust the schema accordingly",
